{
  "description": "Shared menu merge event fixtures for assignment extraction parity between the desktop analytics client (src/core/menu_assignment_apply.py) and the Dachnona server (desktop_analytics_app_sync/services/assignment_state.py). Source of truth lives in the analytics repo; the copy in db.dachnona/contracts/ must stay identical.",
  "notes": [
    "expected_assignments entries always carry order_item_id and menu_item_id.",
    "The variant_id key is OMITTED when the event does not specify a variant (v1 basic merges: variant stays whatever it currently is).",
    "variant_id null means the SQL NULL variant (the __NULL_VARIANT__ sentinel normalizes to null).",
    "The is_verified key is OMITTED when the event does not specify verification state.",
    "is_verified in an extracted assignment is a CREATE-ONLY SEED on the merge stream: the applier (client apply_assignments / server _guarded_assignment_write) writes it only when materializing a previously nonexistent assignment row, and never on an UPDATE to an existing row. The mapping-verification stream is the sole owner of the flag on existing rows (plan I5). These fixtures pin EXTRACTION parity only: both extractors still carry is_verified identically, so expected_assignments is unchanged by that apply-layer rule.",
    "expected_assignments null means the event is not derivable and the applier must fall back / reject."
  ],
